{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Executable signal commands hidden in quoted substitutions or unquoted heredocs bypass the new warning check, though these forms are uncommon for sending signals."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A signal call inside a JavaScript template interpolation bypasses the new warning check, but that form is a contrived way to send a signal."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The standard --eval=CODE syntax bypasses the new warning check and is a realistic alternative to the separately quoted form."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"outage","trigger":"normal","reason":"The new sandbox denies writes to the usual Codex state directory, preventing normal tool-enabled Codex agents from initializing."}]}